  "work_package": "OA (Phase C wave 4): OPENSWATHALGO and OpenSWATH data access",
  "method": "Port of the OPENSWATHALGO headers (DataStructures, ISpectrumAccess, ITransition, Transitions, TransitionExperiment, TransitionHelper, SwathMap, SpectrumHelpers, MockObjects, DataFrameWriter, Scoring, StatsHelpers) and of ANALYSIS/OPENSWATH/DATAACCESS (SpectrumAccessOpenMS, SpectrumAccessOpenMSInMemory, SpectrumAccessTransforming, SpectrumAccessQuadMZTransforming, SpectrumAccessSqMass, SimpleOpenMSSpectraAccessFactory, DataAccessHelper, MRMFeatureAccessOpenMS) plus OpenSwathHelper and SpectrumAddition. Every class-test section at the pin is transcribed with its literals; TEST_REAL_SIMILAR is replayed with relative/absolute tolerance 1e-5. Five files differ between the local core checkout HEAD and the pin (DataStructures.h, ISpectrumAccess.h, SpectrumAccessSqMass.h/.cpp and SpectrumAccessSqMass_test.cpp); they were read and hashed from the pin blobs. All other sources are identical at HEAD and at the pin.",
  "evidence_tier": "tier 3 (transcribed class-test literals: Datastructures_test, SwathMap_test, Scoring_test, StatsHelpers_test, SpectrumAccessOpenMS_test, SpectrumAccessOpenMSInMemory_test, SpectrumAccessQuadMZTransforming_test, SpectrumAccessSqMass_test over the retained SqliteMassFile_1.sqMass, MRMFeatureAccessOpenMS_test, OpenSwathHelper_test, SpectrumAddition_test); tier 4 (independently derived invariants and native guards for everything the class tests do not cover). The only tier-1 run of this group is the OpenSwathHelper::sampleExperiment one noted below. Group O integration added one tier-1 run for OpenSwathHelper::sampleExperiment (../oracle/integ-O-helper: seven seeded runs over a 60-compound library, 548 records, ibminode06, Release install openms4-release-bc9cc12-c19e494-174b576, g++ 14.4.0, run twice byte-identical), replayed record for record by oracle_sample_experiment in tests/openswath_data_access.rs; the TargetedExperiment overload of selectSwathTransitions is tier 3 (OpenSwathHelper_test.cpp lines 58-82).",
